  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 157 AM MDT Sat Aug 15 2026\n\nMonday...A drier pattern ensues and is on tap as the flow aloft \nturns west northwest and the precipitable water values decrease, due \nto drying at low and mid levels and downslope southwest winds near \nthe surface. Thus, a much drier day when compared to the weekend. A \nwarming trend begins with more sunshine and warmer mid level \ntemperatures near 17C at 700 mb.\n\nTuesday...Brisk northwest flow aloft prevails, and with a decent \namount of low and mid level moisture availability as seen in the 12Z \nGFS run, expect isolated to widely scattered late day showers and \nthunderstorms, mainly east of Interstate 25 and the Laramie Range \nduring the afternoon, with coverage everywhere in the evening. \nSimilar maximum temperatures to Monday based on 700 mb temperatures.\n\nWednesday...The synoptic pattern looks more like September and early \nautumn with a deep shortwave trough aloft sweeping across the \nDakotas into western Minnesota by evening, with a much cooler \nairmass moving southward across the northern Rockies, as well as the \nnorthern and central Great Plains, including the Dakotas and much of \nNebraska behind a cold front. Maximum temperatures for our neck of \nthe woods will be quite comfortable with readings in the mid 70s to \nlower 80s, perhaps even cooler than this if the Canadian cool surge \nlies further west. From experience, and from the model trends, this \ntype of cold frontal passage is typically mostly dry for our \nforecast area, and for consistency sake, and matching up with our \nneighboring offices, we will continue with scattered showers and \nthunderstorms in the afternoon and evening for now, though suspect \nthat later shifts will see far less POPS as models come to more \ncongruency and consistency.\n\nThursday-Friday...Models suggest a return to bone dry and hotter \nconditions as the ridge aloft transitions across the northern and \ncentral Rockies and our counties. 700 mb temperatures rise from near \n14C at 00Z/Friday to 18Z at 00Z/Saturday yielding maximum \ntemperatures mainly in the 80s for Thursday, with some 5 to 10 \ndegrees of warming for Friday. Another hot and dry period, \nstretching into the weekend,is on tap.",
